�գ�<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openai/codex/rust-v0.159.2/codex-rs/core/config.schema.json>\r\n131: - Grok Build subagents��project rules��<https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/blob/main/crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/docs/user-guide/16-subagents.md>��<https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build/blob/main/crates/codegen/xai-grok-pager/docs/user-guide/12-project-rules.md>\r\n132: - Kimi Code agents��<https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/agents.html>\r\n133: - OMP task discovery��context��<https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/main/docs/task-agent-discovery.md>��<https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/blob/main/docs/context-files.md>\r\nPATH: .trellis/tasks/09-30-evergreen-runtime-validation/prd.md\r\n1: # T06 ���뵱ǰ��ѡ�汾���幤���е�ʵ�ʹ�����ء��׶ο��ƺ�ί��֤�ݣ����ֱ����� hosted ���ա�\r\n2: \r\n3: ## Goal\r\n4: \r\n5: ���뵱ǰ��ѡ�汾���幤���е�ʵ�ʹ�����ء��׶ο��ƺ�ί��֤�ݣ����ֱ����� hosted ���ա�\r\n6: \r\n7: ## Evidence\r\n8: \r\n9: F7���幤���»Ự��δ�⣬��ǰ SHA �� hosted ֤�ݡ� ��ϸ֤�ݼ� ../09-30-evergreen-five-harness-audit/research/audit.md��\r\n10: \r\n11: ## Requirements\r\n12: \r\n13: - R1 ���������֤�ݶ�Ӧ�����⣬����������������\r\n14: - R2 ������ɹ۲������գ�����ʧ����δ��֤�߽硣\r\n15: - R3 ʵʩ����׼�����д��ע�����ù��ߡ�\r\n16: \r\n17: ## Acceptance Criteria\r\n18: \r\n19: - [ ] AC1��ÿ���߷ֱ��¼�汾��ʵ��ѡ��ģ�͡������ļ���planning ״̬��Active task ���С�ʵ�ʹ���Ȩ���� hook/extension/pull ֤�ݣ���Ų���������߽����\r\n20: - [ ] AC2��ֻ�� smoke ���޸Ĳ�Ʒ�ļ��������� start������׼���Σ�д�о��վݽ������� research/��������غ;ܾ�Խ��ֱ��м�¼��\r\n21: - [ ] AC3��Codex ��ȷ V1/V2��V1 ��� max_depth��V2 �������ü���Kimi ���üȶ� coder + role skill��Grok/OMP ʹ�ö�Ӧԭ�� agent ���á�\r\n22: - [ ] AC4���ڻ����ȷ����/PR/workflow ��Ȩ��hosted test/monitor/docs/Required checks ���ѡ SHA һ�£����򱣳� UNVERIFIED��������Զ�˲�����\r\n23: - [ ] AC5��δ�ܵ� Windows WebView�����̡���ʵ��������ƾ�ݡ����� soak ���ָ���δ��֤״̬���幤�� smoke ����Ϊ��Ʒ native ���ա�\r\n24: \r\n25: ## Dependencies\r\n26: \r\n27: T03/T04 ����� T02 ���ո���ͬ�����Ա���֤��ѡ����������Ķ��ȶ������С�T05 δ���Ų����ɱ������ڸǡ�\r\n28: \r\n29: ## Authorization\r\n30: \r\n31: �û��� 2026-09-30 ��ȷ��׼��Ŀ��ʵʩ�������ļ�������� design.md / implement.md��ȫ�����á���ʵƾ��/���ݿ⡢��װ��push��PR��Զ�� workflow���ύ��鵵����Ĭ����Ȩ�ڡ�\r\nPATH: .trellis/spec/guides/index.md\r\n1: # Thinking Guides\r\n2: \r\n3: > **Purpose**: Expand your thinking to catch things you might not have considered.\r\n4: \r\n5: ---\r\n6: \r\n7: ## Why Thinking Guides?\r\n8: \r\n9: **Most bugs and tech debt come from \"didn't think of that\"**, not from lack of skill:\r\n10: \r\n11: - Didn't think about what happens at layer boundaries �� cross-layer bugs\r\n12: - Didn't think about code patterns repeating �� duplicated code everywhere\r\n13: - Didn't think about edge cases �� runtime errors\r\n14: - Didn't think about future maintainers �� unreadable code\r\n15: \r\n16: These guides help you **ask the right questions before coding**.\r\n17: \r\n18: ---\r\n19: \r\n20: ## Available Guides\r\n21: \r\n22: | Guide | Purpose | When to Use |\r\n23: |-------|---------|-------------|\r\n24: | [Code Reuse Thinking Guide](./code-reuse-thinking-guide.md) | Identify patterns and reduce duplication | When you notice repeated patterns |\r\n25: | [Cross-Layer Thinking Guide](./cross-layer-thinking-guide.md) | Think through data flow across layers | Features spanning multiple layers |\r\n26: \r\n27: ---\r\n28: \r\n29: ## Quick Reference: Thinking Triggers\r\n30: \r\n31: ### When to Think About Cross-Layer Issues\r\n32: \r\n33: - [ ] Feature touches 3+ layers (API, Service, Component, Database)\r\n34: - [ ] Data format changes between layers\r\n35: - [ ] Multiple consumers need the same data\r\n36: - [ ] You're not sure where to put some logic\r\n37: - [ ] You are adding an event kind, JSONL record, RPC payload, or config field\r\n38: - [ ] UI / command code starts casting raw payload fields directly\r\n39: - [ ] Real-time summary or Top 1 is derived from a truncated `rows` page instead of the query snapshot `summary`\r\n40: - [ ] You add an `AppFacade` write path (report, targets, alerts, backup) without a Recovery-only `recovery_only` test\r\n41: \r\n42: �� Read [Cross-Layer Thinking Guide](./cross-layer-thinking-guide.md)\r\n43: \r\n44: ### When Changing AI Residential Domains\r\n45: \r\n46: - [ ] Official firewall/allowlist pages say \"do not block\". They are not a contract to inject every listed host into `AI-�ҿ�`.\r\n47: - [ ] Clash `DOMAIN` / `DOMAIN-SUFFIX` match host/SNI only. A path such as `/backend-api/codex/responses` cannot be split from other paths on the same host.\r\n48: - [ ] Values removed from activation must stay in `allPossible*` so old rules and DNS keys are cleaned.\r\n49: - [ ] Do not retire `daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com`. Antigravity `language_server` uses it as `--cloud_code_endpoint`. A missing official firewall line is not evidence that the host is unused.\r\n50: - [ ] Routing rules and residential `nameserver-policy` can be decoupled. Extra sites use `EXTRA_SITES`; `residentialDns: false` means inject `DOMAIN-SUFFIX` / `DOMAIN` only.\r\n51: - [ ] New domains need a real TLS handshake from the intended DNS vantage, not only a host string. CDN/GeoDNS (for example ESA) can pick a broken edge on residential DoH while airport-upstream DoH works.\r\n52: - [ ] `routing.extra` is a category gate. Site switches are separate flat keys such as `routing.extra_anyrouter`.\r\n53: \r\n54: �� Product contract: [docs/routing-scope.md](../../../docs/routing-scope.md)\r\n55: \r\n56: ### When to Think About Code Reuse\r\n57: \r\n58: - [ ] You're writing similar code to something that exists\r\n59: - [ ] You see the same pattern repeated 3+ times\r\n60: - [ ] You're adding a new field to multiple places\r\n61: - [ ] **You're modifying any constant or config**\r\n62: - [ ] **You're creating a new utility/helper function** �� Search first!\r\n63: - [ ] Two files read the same untyped payload field with local casts\r\n64: - [ ] Multiple branches update the same derived state from `kind` / `action`\r\n65: \r\n66: �� Read [Code Reuse Thinking Guide](./code-reuse-thinking-guide.md)\r\n67: \r\n68: ### When Verifying AI Cross-Review Results\r\n69: \r\n70: - [ ] Reviewer claims \"user input can be malicious\" �� Check the actual data source (internal manifest? user config? external API?)\r\n71: - [ ] Reviewer flags \"missing validation\" �� Is the data from a trusted internal source?\r\n72: - [ ] Reviewer says \"behavior change\" �� Read the code comments �� is it intentional design?\r\n73: - [ ] Reviewer identifies a \"bug\" in test �� Mentally delete the feature being tested �� does the test still pass? If yes �� tautological test\r\n74: \r\n75: **Common AI reviewer false-positive patterns**:\r\n76: 1. **Trust boundary confusion**: Treating internal data (bundled JSON manifests) as untrusted external input\r\n77: 2. **Ignoring design comments**: Flagging intentional behavior documented in code comments as bugs\r\n78: 3. **Variable misreading**: Not tracing a variable to its actual definition (e.g., Map keyed by path vs name)\r\n79: \r\n80: **Verification rule**: Every CRITICAL/WARNING finding must be verified against the actual code before prioritizing. Budget ~35% false-positive rate for AI reviews.\r\n81: \r\n82: ---\r\n83: \r\n84: ## Pre-Modification Rule (CRITICAL)\r\n85: \r\n86: > **Before changing ANY value, ALWAYS search first!**\r\n87: \r\n88: ```bash\r\n89: # Search for the value you're about to change\r\n90: grep -r \"value_to_change\" .\r\n91: ```\r\n92: \r\n93: This single habit prevents most \"forgot to update X\" bugs.\r\n94: \r\n95: ---\r\n96: \r\n97: ## How to Use This Directory\r\n98: \r\n99: 1. **Before coding**: Skim the relevant thinking guide\r\n100: 2. **During coding**: If something feels repetitive or complex, check the guides\r\n101: 3. **After bugs**: Add new insights to the relevant guide (learn from mistakes)\r\n102: \r\n103: ---\r\n104: \r\n105: ## Contributing\r\n106: \r\n107: Found a new \"didn't think of that\" moment? Add it to the relevant guide.\r\n108: \r\n109: ---\r\n110: \r\n111: **Core Principle**: 30 minutes of thinking saves 3 hours of debugging.\r\nPATH: .codex/agents/trellis-research.toml\r\n1: name = \"trellis-research\"\r\n2: description = \"Trellis researcher for specs, code patterns, and affected files. Writes findings into {TASK_DIR}/research/ �� read-only elsewhere.\"\r\n3: sandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\r\n4: # model = \"gpt-5.6-terra\"\r\n5: # model_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\r\n6: \r\n7: developer_instructions = \"\"\"\r\n8: You are the Trellis researcher agent.\r\n9: \r\n10: ## Core principle\r\n11: \r\n12: Conversations get compacted; files don't. Every research topic MUST be\r\n13: persisted to `{TASK_DIR}/research/<topic>.md`. Returning findings only\r\n14: through the chat reply is a failure.\r\n15: \r\n16: ## Trellis Context Loading Protocol\r\n17: \r\n18: - First look for `Full hook output saved to: <path>` in your input above. If\r\n19:   present, the visible `SubagentStart` output was truncated; read the referenced\r\n20:   file before doing research work.\r\n21: - If the referenced file cannot be read, use the active-task fallback below.\r\n22: - If there is no saved-output notice and the\r\n23:   `<!-- trellis-hook-injected -->` marker is present, the hook supplied the\r\n24:   complete `Active task: <path>` header and research-only context.\r\n25: - If there is no saved-output notice and the marker is absent, use the\r\n26:   active-task fallback below.\r\n27: - For the fallback, find `Active task: <path>` in your dispatch prompt. If it\r\n28:   is absent too, ask the main session for the path; do not run\r\n29:   `task.py current`, guess, or use another session's task.\r\n30: - Do not load `implement.jsonl` or `check.jsonl`; research is role-isolated.\r\n31: \r\n32: ## Workflow\r\n33: \r\n34: 1. Use the active task path supplied by the context-loading protocol. If no\r\n35:    path is supplied, ask the user where to write output; do not guess.\r\n36: 2. Run `mkdir -p <TASK_DIR>/research` to ensure the directory exists.\r\n37: 3. Read `.trellis/workflow.md`, relevant `.trellis/spec/` files, and\r\n38:    target code before forming an opinion.\r\n39: 4. For each research topic, write `<TASK_DIR>/research/<slug>.md` with:\r\n40:    - Query, scope, date\r\n41:    - Files found (path + one-line description)\r\n42:    - Code patterns (cite file:line)\r\n43:    - External references (docs, versions)\r\n44:    - Related specs\r\n45:    - Caveats / not-found notes\r\n46: 5. Reply with only: list of files written, one-line summary per file,\r\n47:    any critical caveats. Do not paste full research into the reply.\r\n48: \r\n49: ## Scope limits\r\n50: \r\n51: Write allowed ONLY in `{TASK_DIR}/research/`.\r\n52: \r\n53: Write forbidden everywhere else:\r\n54: - Code files (`src/`, `lib/`, ��)\r\n55: - Spec files (`.trellis/spec/`) �� use `update-spec` skill instead\r\n56: - `.trellis/scripts/`, `.trellis/workflow.md`, platform config\r\n57: - Other task directories\r\n58: - Any git operation\r\n59: \r\n60: If the user asks you to edit code, decline and tell them to spawn the\r\n61: `implement` agent.\r\n62: \r\n63: ## Output format for each research file\r\n64: \r\n65: ```\r\n66: # Research: <topic>\r\n67: \r\n68: - Query: ...\r\n69: - Scope: internal / external / mixed\r\n70: - Date: YYYY-MM-DD\r\n71: \r\n72: ## Findings\r\n73: ...\r\n74: \r\n75: ## Caveats / Not Found\r\n76: ...\r\n77: ```\r\n78: \"\"\"\r\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}}
